 { As we were taught when beginners, in such positions before pushing the pawn we should improve our king. } 1. { -KEY- } Kf3 $1 ( 1. Kg3 { is also good, as well as 2.Kg4 (or 2.Ke4) on the next move. } ) 
 ( { Only a very inexperienced player would consider } 1. f4 $2 { or } 1. f3 $2 { , after which a draw is inevitable. } ) 
Kf7 2. Kf4 Kf6 3. f3 $1 { A clever waiting move. } ( { White wins after } 3. f3 Ke6 4. Kg5 ) 
 ( { or } 3. f3 Kg6 4. Ke5 { further improving the king. } ) 
 
