2. f5 ( { Black also draws after } 2. e4 Kh3 3. e5 Kh4 4. e6 Bb4 ) 
 ( { or } 2. Kg4 $5 Kg2 3. e4 Kf2 4. e5 Ke3 5. f5 Bc3 6. e6 Bf6 $1 7. Kh5 Kd4 8. Kg6 Ke5 { In the latter variation, we can see that Black has saved a tempo upon the subline 1...Bd2 above. } ) 
Kh3 3. f6 Kh4 4. Kf4 ( { Seeing that } 4. f7 Bb4 { is useless, White tries obstructing the enemy king, just like in the previous example. } ) 
Kh5 5. Kf5 Kh6 6. e4 Kh7 $1 { The king's journey still isn't over - its ideal destiny is f8 or e8. } 7. e5 ( { The game actually went } 7. Ke6 Kg6 8. e5 Bb4 { and, incapable of progress, White agreed to a draw. } ) 
Kg8 8. e6 Kf8 { White can't win; } ( { e.g. } 8... Kf8 9. Ke4 { (heading for d7) } Bc3 { or } 9. Kg6 Bb4 ) 

