 { Such pawn endings on a single flank with an extra pawn - leaving aside the case with a single pawn - are usually won quite easily. However, it is imperative to improve the king as much as possible before advancing the pawns. } 1. { -KEY- } Kg3 $1 { In order to improve properly, the king should make a turn to the other side of the pawns. } ( { In contrast, after } 1. Kg5 $6 Kg7 2. f5 $2 gxf5 3. Kxf5 Kf7 { Black draws. } ) 
Kf7 2. Kf3 Ke7 ( { Or } 2... Kf6 3. Ke4 Ke6 { transposing. } ) 
3. Ke3 { Applying distant opposition, an idea that we will study more thoroughly in the next section. } ( { The simple } 3. Ke4 { was also good; e.g. } Kf6 4. Kd5 Kf7 5. Ke5 Ke7 6. g5 { again transposing to the main line. } ) 
Kd7 4. Ke4 Ke6 ( { Or } 4... Kd6 5. Kd4 $1 Ke6 6. Kc5 { and the white king enters anyway. But not } 5. f5 $2 Ke7 $1 ) 
5. g5 { The king can no longer be improved, so it is time to use a pawn move in order to gain the opposition. } Kd6 ( { If } 5... Ke7 { then } 6. Ke5 { while other moves are met by 6.Kd5. } ) 
6. f5 $1 ( { Just in time; when the black king can't reach f7 after } 6. f5 gxf5 7. Kxf5 ) 
Ke7 7. f6+ $1 ( { But not } 7. fxg6 $2 Kf8 8. Ke5 Kg7 9. Kf5 Kg8 10. Kf6 Kf8 11. g7 Kg8 { with a draw. It is worth noting that with the g5 pawn still on g4, White could indeed win here by } 12. Kf5 $1 Kxg7 { and now 13.Kg5. } ) 
Kf7 8. Ke5 Kf8 9. f7 $1 { This pawn sacrifice is the only winning idea; After 9.f7 Black resigned, but let's see a possible conclusion of the game. } ( { which could also be realized by } 9. Ke6 Ke8 10. f7 Kf8 11. Kd6 $1 { etc. } ) 
Kxf7 10. Kd6 { A final 'improvement' measure, in order to conquer the g6-pawn. } Kf8 11. Ke6 Kg7 12. Ke7 Kg8 13. Kf6 Kh7 14. Kf7 Kh8 15. Kxg6 { Returning to the subject of key squares, with a pawn on the fifth rank (from Black's perspective, the fourth) these squares are located one rank closer to the pawn, in this case f6, g6, and h6. } ( { So White wins no matter who is to move; e.g. } 15. Kxg6 Kg8 16. Kh6 { avoiding any stalemate scenarios } Kh8 17. g6 Kg8 18. g7 ) 

