 { Another type of ending where the 'King first!' idea holds great importance is the one with rook vs. pawns. Here is an example.Despite appearances White is just in time to save a draw, if he uses his king first. } 1. { -KEY- } Ke5 $1 { Improving the king while obstructing its black counterpart. } ( { In contrast, after } 1. c6 $2 Kf5 $1 2. Kd5 Rd2 $1 3. Kc5 Ke6 { the black king approaches the pawn with decisive effect. } ) 
