 ( { Changing the move order with } 1... Rh1 2. Kg5 Kd4 $1 3. Kg6 Ke5 { was possible as well. } ) 
2. h6 Rh1 3. Kg5 Ke5 $1 { Again, the king should approach the more dangerous pawn whenever possible. } 4. Kg6 Ke6 5. h7 ( { After } 5. c5 Rg1 6. Kh7 Kf7 { etc - Speelman } ) 
 ( { or } 5. Kg7 Ke7 $1 6. h7 Rg1 7. Kh8 Kf7 { Black also wins. Interestingly, in the second line the c pawn works against White, who would have been stalemated without it. } ) 
